# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local datasets and run outputs. These must stay ignored, not merely uncommitted.
#
# Anything that stages the working tree -- `git add -A`, `git add .`, the IDE's "Stage All
# Changes", `git stash -u` -- walks every untracked file. A file above
# core.bigFileThreshold (512 MB by default) is not written as a loose object: git streams
# it straight into a new pack via the bulk-checkin path. Interrupt that and the partial
# pack is orphaned as .git/objects/pack/tmp_pack_XXXXXX, which nothing ever cleans up --
# `git gc` only warns "garbage found". 1,603 such orphans had grown .git to 281 GB.
#
# i24_motion_source_data holds single 25 GB JSONs, so one stray `git add -A` is enough.
# Below 512 MB the failure just changes shape: git writes a multi-hundred-MB loose object
# per file instead, so the sweep's 132 logs still cannot go in here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Source data and preprocessing products
i24motion_macro_micro/i24_motion_source_data/
i24motion_macro_micro/preprocessing_data/
i24motion_macro_micro/preprocessing_data_100m_1s/
i24motion_macro_micro/11-30-2022/
i24motion_macro_micro/simulation_dataset/

# Simulation / sweep / RL outputs
i24motion_macro_micro/simplified_scenario_tests/verification_results*/
i24motion_macro_micro/simplified_scenario_tests/figure_runs*/
i24motion_macro_micro/run_data/
i24motion_macro_micro/junk_output/

